# Product Marketplace API

## Overview
This project is a **backend application** for managing products in a business context. Built with **Django and Django REST Framework (DRF)**, it allows businesses to create, update, and manage products, with an approval workflow before products become public. 

Key features include:
- CRUD operations for products
- Product approval workflow (`draft`, `pending`, `approved`)
- Business association for products
- User-based ownership of products
- Timestamped product creation

This backend serves as the foundation for a product management system, which can later integrate with a frontend application.

---

## Technologies Used
- **Python 3.11+** – Core programming language
- **Django 4.x** – Backend web framework
- **Django REST Framework (DRF)** – RESTful API development 
- **SQLite** (development database)
- **Git** – Version control and collaboration

---

## Getting Started

### 1. Clone the repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/baisoft-product-marketplace/backend.git
cd backend

## 2. Create a virtual Environment
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate   # Linux/macOS
venv\Scripts\activate      # Windows

## 3. Install dependencies 
pip install -r requirements.txt

## 4.Apply database migrations
python manage.py migrate

## 5. Run the development server 
python manage.py runserver
The backend will be accessible at http://localhost:8000/

## 6. Implementation Details

Product Model

Fields: name, description, price, status, business, created_by, created_at

Status workflow: draft → pending → approved

ProductViewSet

Handles authenticated CRUD operations for products

Only owners of products can modify them

Uses DRF ModelViewSet with proper permissions

PublicProductViewSet

Read-only view for listing approved products

Accessible to all users without authentication

Routing

Uses DefaultRouter to automatically register products and public/products endpoints

